## 12. Principal risks and required mitigations

| Risk | Failure mode | Required mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| O06 stale specification | Correct implementation fails one oracle or follows wrong history behavior | Merge normative correction first; generate expected states from manifest |
| Logical/physical viewport split | Offset hits, DPI-dependent scale, wrong depth UV, resize jump | One immutable viewport snapshot owned by P6 and shared through render submission |
| Reverse-Z transcription | Grid/gizmo occlusion inverted | Explicit projection/depth convention in CPU and shader; forward/reverse fake tests |
| Reference active state under-specified | Invented active color presented as parity | Capture V02 native active frames; keep state token separate from visual mapping until then |
| Negative/non-uniform/singular parent | Reflected axes, NaN, transform jump, wrong local delta | Double-precision math, condition/finiteness checks, deterministic fail-closed tests |
| Focus/capture ambiguity | Lost release, double commit, camera starts moving | Ordered application-visible events, latched state, opaque capture token, exact-once transaction ID |
| Native wide-line reliance | Different thickness/coverage on D3D12/Metal/mobile GPUs | Shader-expanded triangle quads and logical-pixel tests |
| Sampling scene depth while self-depth testing | Feedback/layout hazard or gizmo parts draw through each other | Separate helper depth attachment plus PassExecutor-declared scene-depth ShaderRead |
| Resize lifetime | Use-after-free or device idle in interactive path | RHI logical handles, deferred retirement, per-frame table discipline, fake/Vulkan validation |
| Android target contamination | Desktop editor symbols/dependencies in viewer | Desktop-only source/target wiring plus active-CMake and final-symbol tests |
| Scene-root shortcut | Wrong baseline/history/selection behavior | Explicit routing guard and dedicated R13 non-history tests |
| Reference helper reuse | RHI/platform/license boundary violation | Behavior-only evidence; MGIF-owned CPU/RHI implementation; zero forbidden dependencies |

## 13. Explicit non-claims

This report makes all of the following explicit:

- It is **not** an implementation, a build result, a test result, a screenshot comparison, or a Gate P7 PASS.
- It does not claim the current MGIF worktree is clean, reproducibly buildable, or baseline-green; no build/test was authorized or run.
- It does not claim F19 or F20 is implemented. The manifest currently says both are not implemented.
- It does not claim visual parity for geometry, hover, active, depth/x-ray, grid LOD, DPI, or constant pixel size. Required native captures remain evidence debt.
- It does not claim the fixed-reference source probe proves private callback order, private drag state, direct history memory, full UI behavior, Vulkan visuals, or outside-viewport capture.
- It does not claim that same-frame Escape plus release commits. The authoritative target is the manifest's no-history visible result; the locked task text must be corrected.
- It does not claim a visible Local space, screen-rotation handle, mutually exclusive translate/rotate/scale mode, or Gizmo cancel/rollback API. Those are not fixed-reference P7 behavior.
- It does not claim scene-root transforms are controlled by the node gizmo or enter history. They remain a separate baseline-driven non-history route.
- It does not claim Metal runtime capability or D3D12 runtime parity. Metal is unavailable/scaffold-only in the audited implementation; D3D12/Metal scope is public/compile contract evidence.
- It does not claim Android provides or should provide desktop editor UI/overlay. Mobile-shaped viewport visual tests run in the desktop Vulkan acceptance application.
- It does not claim current RHI line-width semantics are portable. The proposal deliberately uses triangle-expanded lines.
- It does not claim an RHI API extension is unnecessary under every implementation outcome. It says the currently audited public surface appears sufficient; any discovered gap requires an RHI-level cross-backend review, never a native escape hatch.
- It does not copy, port, wrap, link, expose, or authorize reference Vulkan helpers or any `nvcore`, `nvpro`, `nvapp`, `nvgui`, `nvvk*`, or `nvvkgltf` production dependency.
- It does not authorize a Dear ImGui fork or override. Production remains pinned upstream Dear ImGui plus MGIF-owned adapters only.

## 14. Final readiness decision

The RHI foundation is **conditionally adequate**, but P7 as a product slice is **not ready to implement or sign off**. The immediate blockers are the O06 normative contradiction, missing P5/P6/transaction contracts, unresolved viewport/DPI mapping, incomplete native visual baselines, and absent P7/fake-RHI test surfaces.

Once the O06 text is corrected and P5/P6 freeze the proposed revisioned viewport/input/data-flow boundaries, P7-T01 through P7-T03 can proceed clean-room with no reference-helper or native RHI dependency. P7-T04 must use the manifest state machine in this report, and P7-T05/Gate P7 remain evidence-producing stages rather than assumptions.
